<article class="env-lemma" id="0CZP">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0CZP">Lemma <span data-tag="0CZP">31.36.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a finite type quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_ S$-module. Let $Z_ k \subset S$ be the closed subscheme cut out by $\text{Fit}_ k(\mathcal{F})$, see Section <a href="/tag/0C3C" data-tag="0C3C">31.9</a>. Let $S' \to S$ be the blowup of $S$ in $Z_ k$ and let $\mathcal{F}'$ be the strict transform of $\mathcal{F}$. Then $\mathcal{F}'$ can locally be generated by $\leq k$ sections. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Recall that $\mathcal{F}'$ can locally be generated by $\leq k$ sections if and only if $\text{Fit}_ k(\mathcal{F}') = \mathcal{O}_{S'}$, see Lemma <a href="/tag/0C3F" data-tag="0C3F">31.9.4</a>. Hence this lemma is a translation of More on Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0CZM" data-tag="0CZM">15.27.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>